A field a body written empty would copy into one that does not accept every
value of it: the copy is refused (E0358), and the struct holding it is not
then reported as one the target lacks, since the target declares it.
-- ship/history/0.0.thema --
Schema: {
	meta: {
		count: int
		x:     string
	}
}
-- ship/history/1.0.thema --
Schema: {
	meta: {
		count: int & <10
		x:     string
		owner: string
	}
}

ForwardLens: {
	v0_0: _
	v1_0: {
		meta: {
			owner: "nobody"
		}
	}
}
-- ship/tip.thema --
Schema: {
	meta: {
		count: int & <10
		x:     string
		owner: string
	}
}
-- out/error --
error[E0358]: the ForwardLens of v1.0 would copy v0_0.meta.count into meta.count, which does not accept every value of it
  --> history/1.0.thema:12:3
   |
12 |         meta: {
   |         ^^^^
   |
   = note: both v0.0 and v1.0 declare meta.count, so a lens that does not map it copies it
   = note: meta.count in v1.0 is now int & <10, which does not accept every value of the prior int
   = help: map meta.count in the ForwardLens: a _match, a computed value, or a constant
